{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TBetaMarkovCollapseGeneralLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TBetaMarkovCollapseGeneralLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.markov_frobenius_min_norm_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.markov_frobenius_min_norm_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L231-L277","doc":"**T_β = S · 1 uniqueness — equality case of the min-norm bound.**\n\nCompanion to `markov_frobenius_min_norm_lift`.  Under the same\nconstraint `τ(X) = S` plus PSD + non-degeneracy of `τ` on\nsquares, the equality `τ(X · X) = S²` holds iff `X = S · 1`.\n\nCombined with `markov_frobenius_min_norm_lift`, this gives the\nfull SHAPE-collapse claim: the minimum-Frobenius-norm\nprimal-feasible element is `T_β = S · 1`, attained uniquely.\n\nProof sketch:\n- (⇒) `τ(X*X) = S²` + completing_the_square + constraint ⇒\n  `τ((X - S•1)²) = 0` ⇒ `X - S•1 = 0` by NonDegTrace.\n- (⇐) `X = S • 1` ⇒ `τ(X*X) = τ((S•1)*(S•1)) = τ((S²)•1)\n  = S² τ(1) = S²` by NormalizedTrace.tau_one.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-06-03-qbeta-markov-trace-shape-collapse.md\n     §\"Proof — Lagrangian / completing-the-square argument\" ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.markov_frobenius_min_norm_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.markov_frobenius_min_norm_lift","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L191-L229","doc":"**T_β = S · 1 — general algebra min-Frobenius-norm LOWER BOUND.**\n\nUnder the SDP constraint `τ(X) = S` and PSD of `τ` on squares\n(class hypothesis per §3b-cond), the Frobenius norm-squared\n`τ(X · X)` is bounded below by `S²`.\n\nThe companion theorem `markov_frobenius_min_norm_uniqueness`\nbelow (using `NonDegTrace`) establishes that the lower bound is\nattained iff `X = S • 1`, giving the full SHAPE-collapse claim\n`T_β = S · 1_H` of PR #1750.\n\nThis does not apply to `A = H_n(R, q)`, `n ≥ 3`, with `τ = τ_M`,\nwhere `PSDTrace` fails (see the class docstring).  The L2 SHAPE × S\ndecomposition of PR #1739 is basis-dependence of the\ncoordinate-vector Euclidean norm on `ℝ^6`, NOT the categorical\nFrobenius norm on H_3(ℝ, q).\n\nRef: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-06-03-qbeta-markov-trace-shape-collapse.md\n     §\"Categorical reading\" + prop:t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse .md ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse-general","label":"prop:t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse-general","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse-general.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.completing_the_square_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.completing_the_square_general","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L136-L189","doc":"**Completing-the-square algebraic identity (general algebra).**\n\nFor any `X ∈ A`, `S ∈ R`:\n\n$$τ(X · X) = τ((X - S·1)(X - S·1)) + 2 S τ(X) - S².$$\n\nProof reduces to (a) expanding `(X - S•1)·(X - S•1)` via the\nR-algebra ring identities, then (b) applying `τ`'s linearity +\n`τ(S²•1) = S² τ(1) = S²` via normalisation.\n\nMechanical but verbose with the smul-vs-mul expansion\n(`S • X = (algebraMap R A S) * X`) and non-commutative ring\nmanipulation.  Queued as a separate commit on this branch.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-06-03-qbeta-markov-trace-shape-collapse.md\n     §\"Categorical reading\" + prop:t-beta-markov-frobenius-collapse .md\n     §\"Proof — Lagrangian / completing-the-square argument\" ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.smul_one_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.smul_one_sq","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L127-L134","doc":"**Reusable lemma: `(r • 1) * (r • 1) = (r * r) • 1`** in any\nunital R-algebra `A`.  Used in both `completing_the_square_general`\nand `markov_frobenius_min_norm_uniqueness` (reverse direction).\nExtracted per Copilot review #1761 to avoid duplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NonDegTrace.nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NonDegTrace.nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NonDegTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NonDegTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L122-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NonDegTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NonDegTrace","kind":"class","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L107-L125","doc":"**Non-degeneracy on squares.**\n\n`τ(X · X) = 0 ⇒ X = 0`.  Stronger than PSD; equivalent under\nPSD to \"the Frobenius form has trivial radical on squares\".\n\n**Not available for Jones–Markov `τ_M` on `H_n(R, q)` (corrected\n2026-08-09).**  This docstring used to cite `tau_M_non_degenerate`\nin `markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean` as establishing the\nhypothesis.  That declaration is retired: under production\nconvention D, `z = q³/(q²+1)`, the Markov–Frobenius form is\ndegenerate on `H_n(R, q)` for `n ≥ 3`, with radical exactly the\nTemperley–Lieb ideal `I_n`.  The class is satisfied instead by\n`A = TL_n(q) = H_n(q)/I_n`, on which the descended pairing *is*\nnon-degenerate.  The lemmas below are unaffected — they take this\nclass as a hypothesis and never claimed to discharge it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.PSDTrace.psd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.PSDTrace.psd","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.PSDTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.PSDTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.PSDTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.PSDTrace","kind":"class","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L88-L105","doc":"**Frobenius positive-semi-definiteness on squares.**\n\nThe trace `τ` is positive-semi-definite on the Frobenius bilinear\nform `⟨X, Y⟩_τ := τ(X · Y)`, i.e. `0 ≤ τ(X · X)` for every `X`.\n\n**Not satisfied by the Jones–Markov `τ_M` on `H_n(R, q)` for\n`n ≥ 3` (corrected 2026-11-15).**  At `X = σ₁σ₂ − σ₂σ₁ ∈ H₃`,\n`τ_M(X · X) = −2(q⁴ + q² + 1)/(q² + 1)² < 0`.  The positive form on\n`H_n` is the twisted one, `τ_M(X · X†)` with `†` the anti-involution\nfixing each `σ_i`; this class does not encode it.\n\nClass hypothesis per AGENTS.md §3b-cond: the substantive analytic\ncontent is axiomatised here so the downstream min-norm theorem is\nsorry-free **conditional on the class instance**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.tau_cyc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.tau_cyc","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.tau_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.tau_one","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.tau","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovFrobeniusCollapse.General.NormalizedTrace","kind":"structure","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/t-beta-markov-collapse-general-lift.lean#L66-L86","doc":"**Normalized R-linear trace** on a unital R-algebra `A`.\n\nA trace is an R-linear map `τ : A → R` satisfying\n\n- **Normalisation:** `τ(1) = 1`.\n- **Cyclicity (trace property):** `τ(x · y) = τ(y · x)`.\n\nThe Jones–Markov trace `τ_M` on the Iwahori–Hecke algebra `H_n(R, q)`\nis the canonical example (Wenzl 1988, Jones 1987; uniqueness at a\nfixed Ocneanu parameter `z`, and the derivation of `z` itself, in\n`QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovWeights_eq_jones_of_threeRow_eq_zero`).\n\n**Updated 2026-08-09.** This used to cite\n`QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceUniqueness`, retired that day as\nunsatisfiable — see the retraction note at the head of\n`markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}